==Sanskrit==

===Etymology===
Possibly borrowed from {{der|sa|dra-pro|*palam||ripe fruit}}; compare {{cog|ta|பழம்}}, {{cog|ml|പഴം}}, {{cog|te|పండు}} and {{cog|kn|ಹಣ್ಣು}}.

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|tr=phála|g=n}}

# [[fruit]]
# the kernel or seed of a fruit
# a [[nutmeg]]
# the menstrual discharge
# {{lb|sa|figuratively}} fruit, consequence, effect, result, retribution (good or bad), gain or loss, reward or punishment, advantage or disadvantage
# [[benefit]], [[enjoyment]]
# [[compensation]]
# {{lb|sa|rhetoric}} the issue or end of an action
# {{lb|sa|mathematics}} the result of a calculation, product or quotient
# corrective equation
# area or superficial contents of a figure
# interest on capital
# the third term in a rule of three sum
# [[gift]], [[donation]]
# a gaming board
# a blade (of a sword or knife)
# the point of an arrow
# [[shield]]
# a ploughshare
# a point or spot on a die

